=head1 DESCRIPTION

The device-remembering configuration for a user pool.

When you provide a value for any property of C<DeviceConfiguration>,
you activate the device remembering for the user pool.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 ChallengeRequiredOnNewDevice => Bool

When true, a remembered device can sign in with device authentication
instead of SMS and time-based one-time password (TOTP) factors for
multi-factor authentication (MFA).

Whether or not C<ChallengeRequiredOnNewDevice> is true, users who sign
in with devices that have not been confirmed or remembered must still
provide a second factor in a user pool that requires MFA.


=head2 DeviceOnlyRememberedOnUserPrompt => Bool

When true, Amazon Cognito doesn't automatically remember a user's
device when your app sends a C<ConfirmDevice> API request. In your app,
create a prompt for your user to choose whether they want to remember
their device. Return the user's choice in an C<UpdateDeviceStatus> API
request.

When C<DeviceOnlyRememberedOnUserPrompt> is C<false>, Amazon Cognito
immediately remembers devices that you register in a C<ConfirmDevice>
API request.



